# Native binaries (.so files) - NOT in git, NOT in the npm tarball.
#
# Distribution flow (v1.5.14+):
#   1. Release workflow builds/packs jniLibs/ + .sha256 into a tarball.
#   2. Workflow uploads <jniLibs.tar.gz> + <jniLibs.tar.gz.sha256> as
#      GitHub Release assets for tag v*.*.*.
#   3. The lib's `scripts/download-native.js` (invoked by `postinstall`
#      in package.json) downloads the matching version's tarball from
#      the GitHub Release during `npm install`, verifies the SHA-256,
#      and extracts into this directory.
#
# Why not commit: ~152 MB across 4 ABIs would bloat every clone forever.
# This is the llama.rn pattern (https://github.com/mybigday/llama.rn) —
# the industry-standard approach for RN libs shipping prebuilt natives.
#
# Idempotency: download-native.js skips if
#   android/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libmpv.so already exists.
android/src/main/jniLibs/

# TypeScript build outputs
src/lib/
src/es/
*.tsbuildinfo

